// =====================================================================
// Property templates — Spiking Entropy Coder archetype
// Companion to research/compression/spiking_entropy_coder.typ
//
// Two classes, matching the note's §6/§7 split:
//   (A) STRUCTURAL / SAFETY     — hold for ANY predictor q (correctness)
//   (B) QUANTITATIVE / OPTIMALITY — predictor-dependent (the thing learning
//                                   improves; near-entropy cost)
//
// Labels assumed (instantiate against a concrete model, e.g. a DTMC over the
// momentum-rover source coupled to a 4-neuron temporal-WTA readout, in the
// style of research/contralateral-inhibition/contra_inhib_fixed.prism):
//   "win_i"   : readout neuron i fired first this symbol window  (i in 1..4)
//   "winner"  : sum over i of win_i  (number of winners this window)
//   "decoded" : symbol id elected by the WTA
//   "emitted" : true source symbol x_t for this window
//   reward "time" : per-window latency  -lambda*log2 q(x_t | c_t)
//                   (continuous; in a pure DTMC use a spike-COUNT proxy and
//                    accept the timing-resolution penalty — see note §7 check)
// =====================================================================


// ── (A) STRUCTURAL / SAFETY — independent of predictor quality ───────

// A1: Mutual exclusion — at most one winner per symbol (unambiguous decode).
//     A bad predictor may be SLOW but never AMBIGUOUS.
P>=1 [ G (winner <= 1) ]

// A2: Liveness — every symbol window eventually elects a winner
//     (decoding terminates; the code is complete / decodable).
P>=1 [ G F (winner = 1) ]

// A3: Losslessness — the decoded symbol always equals the emitted one.
//     This is the safety core: decode(encode(x)) = x for all streams.
P>=1 [ G (decoded = emitted) ]

// A4: Prefix-freeness (self-clocking) — a winner resets the layer before the
//     next window's integration begins; no two windows' spikes interleave.
//     Structural guard-level invariant; stated as a reachability sanity check.
P>=1 [ G (winner = 1 => X (winner = 0 U "new_window")) ]


// ── (B) QUANTITATIVE / OPTIMALITY — predictor-dependent ──────────────

// B1: Expected per-symbol cost (steady state). Compare against the closed-form
//     entropy-rate floor H_rate = 0.9782 bits/symbol (momentum rover, s=0.7,
//     from validate.py). Optimality target:  R["time"] <= lambda*(H_rate + eps).
R{"time"}=? [ S ]

// B2: Expected cost to absorb a length-N stream (transient form), for finite
//     verification against H_rate*N.  (Set up an absorbing "done" state.)
R{"time"}=? [ F "done" ]

// B3: Stupidity tax made checkable. Run B1 for the LEARNED predictor q and for
//     the memoryless baseline q=pi; the difference is lambda*D_KL(p||q_pi).
//     For the rover: memoryless cost - floor = 0.7718 bits/symbol (validate.py).
//     A learning step is "an improvement" iff it lowers R{"time"}=?[S].

// B4: Sanity bounds (Shannon source-coding theorem, physical form):
//     floor  <=  R{"time"}=?[S]/lambda  <  floor + (timing-resolution penalty).
//     In continuous time the classic "+1 bit" upper slack collapses (note Thm 2);
//     the residual slack is the analog timing penalty (note §4 honesty check).


// ── Notes ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// * A1+A2 together are the WTA "always eventually EXACTLY one winner" pair the
//   contralateral-inhibition study already proves — reused verbatim here as the
//   coder's correctness backbone.
// * The clean separation A (predictor-free) vs B (predictor-dependent) is the
//   formal-methods payoff: correctness is certified once, optimality is the
//   quantity training drives down. They never trade off.
